\ main.6502 - Dare Devil Denis 2: four strips of the original, each an endless runner.
\
\ LAYER 4.3 (PLAN.md): the jump, collisions, the crash, respawn and takes. Each player has two
\ keys, accelerate and jump (decision 7), measured in jsbeeb (docs/done.md layer 4.2): Z X | V B
\ | M , | . /, one key in each of matrix columns 1-8. Letting go of accelerate slows the rider by 1
\ a field (decision 24, PROPOSED). Each rider has its own colours (decision 17). No enemies, gold,
\ wages or level types yet (layers 4.4, 4.5): every strip is drawn as land.
\
\ THE MACHINE. Loaded at &1900 by *RUN, it copies itself down to &0E00 (`reloc`, last in the
\ file) over the DFS's workspace, and never touches the disc again. The MOS sets MODE 2 and turns
\ the cursor off; then IRQ1V is ours (the kit's irq.6502): the MOS's interrupts stop, and the
\ keys are read straight off the System VIA (the kit's keydown.6502).
\
\ THE SCREEN is the original's MODE 2 (docs/sequel.md). Strip k's WINDOW is character rows 4+7k
\ to 9+7k, 48 lines: lines 0-23 sky (black), 24-39 the obstacle rows (7+7k, 8+7k), 40-47 the
\ ground row (9+7k), whose top four lines are lit and the same at every column, so the ground is
\ drawn once and only holes change it. A rider on the ground has its top at window line 24; a
\ jump raises it to line 4 at most (20 lines, the original's peak).
\
\ THE TIMING (decision 12). The VSync interrupt starts System VIA T1, which fires as the raster
\ leaves each strip's ground row - first 120 scanlines after the VSync edge (MODE 2: R7 = 34, so
\ the display starts 40 lines after it), then every 56 - and counts `bands`. The main loop
\ updates strip k only once `bands` > k in this field: the raster has passed its whole window and
\ will not be back for about 260 lines (33,000 cycles).
\
\ THE SCROLL. Each strip has a course position `pos` (the course column at screen column 0), in
\ 16.8 fixed point. Per field: pos += vel / 256, then vel += 1 with accelerate held, up to 250 -
\ the original's motion (update_player: x += vel x 3 / 256 and vel += 3, once every 3 fields) at
\ 3 times the rate and a third of the step (decision 16). A move of one column means, for each
\ object on screen:
\   obstacle   its shift routine (make_data.py): only the bytes that differ from one column right
\   hole       open its new left column, close the column it left (col + w)
\ Objects come off `first`, the first not yet gone off the left, in course order.
\
\ THE RIDER (update_player, transliterated). The jump starts from the ground with jump held and
\ lasts JUMP_FIELDS fields, the height from jump_h (the original's arc, make_data.py). The rider
\ is drawn whole (its black included, as the original's plot_sprite does) at RIDER, over the
\ rider's four columns of whatever is under it: black sky, or the obstacle there (restore_under).
\ Then the original's collision reads, of the SCREEN, as the original does (main_game_loop,
\ check_for_collision): with the rider's top at line t, a lit byte at column RIDER+4 on line t+15
\ (plot_sprite's right_edge), t+8 (middle right) or t-1 (top right); in the air, a lit byte under
\ its left column (t+16); on the ground, an unlit ground byte under its left column (a hole:
\ decision 6, a crash, where the original's rider fell to the next ground).
\
\ THE CRASH (kill_player; measured, tools/measure_crash.mjs): the explosion at the rider, the
\ dead rider flying off right and down for 42 fields, lying there 140 fields; then the next take
\ (the original has 3: `take` 1-3, out at 4), or out (decision 8). The strip does not move. The
\ original's clapperboard screen goes. RESPAWN (decision 8 says past the hazard; decision 26,
\ PROPOSED, says where): standing, at the first course column past the crash with 16 columns
\ clear - the rider's four and 12 ahead. It takes two fields: the old picture erased, then the
\ new one drawn. A take comes back as the rider reaches each sea level, 2, 5 ... 35, if one has
\ been lost (consider_gaining_extra_take).
\
\   strip_go .. strip_done      one strip's update (X = strip), for a cycle-count breakpoint pair
\   keys_go .. keys_done        the eight keys
\   crash_at                    a rider has just crashed (strip in `strip`, the reading in `cause`)

INCLUDE "../../src/lib/beeb.h.6502"

OSWRCH  = oswrch
LOAD_AT = &1900                 \ where *RUN puts the file
ORG_AT  = &0E00                 \ where it runs

SCREEN  = &3000
ROW     = 640                   \ bytes in a MODE 2 character row
RIDER   = 12                    \ the riders' fixed screen column (decision 23, PROPOSED)
VMAX    = 250                   \ the original's velocity cap (update_player)
SKY     = 24                    \ window lines 0-23 are sky; a rider on the ground has its top here
\ the tall sprites' numbers (TALL_*) are make_data.py's, in data.6502
TAKES   = 3                     \ the original's: out when `take` reaches 4
DEAD_COL = 18                   \ where the dead rider ends up, columns right of the rider
LEVEL_COLS = 4 * 76             \ a level: four grounds (decision 18)
CLEAR   = 16                    \ respawn: columns clear from the rider's left column (decision 26)
T1_FIRST = 120 * SL - 4 * SL - 2    \ VSync edge -> band 0 left; the handler runs ~4 lines late
T1_NEXT  = 56 * SL - 2              \ one band to the next (T1 continuous: the latch reloads)


\ zero page: &70-&8F is the user's; &00-&6F is BASIC's, and BASIC never runs
\ enemies.6502's:
ek       = &00                  \ the strip
es       = &01                  \ a slot index (strip x 2 + s)
eg       = &02                  \ an enemy (slot x 6 + e)
eo       = &03                  \ an order index (0-11)
eo_first = &04                  \ the left edge level's slot parity
en_cnt   = &05
el_level = &06
el_start = &07                  \ 2
erider   = &09                  \ an enemy is in the rider's columns
nspan    = &0A
sp_all   = &0B
ro_c     = &0C                  \ erase_box: the old box
ro_t     = &0D
rn_c     = &0E                  \ and the new
rn_t     = &0F
eb_cc    = &10
rl_c     = &11                  \ restore_lines: the column
rl_a     = &12                  \ and the lines
rl_b     = &13
ro_kind  = &14                  \ the obstacle there (&FF none)
ro_oc    = &15                  \ and its column
esp_t    = &16
esp_s    = &17
esp_v    = &18
esp_left = &19
cf_n     = &1A
d16_skip = &1B                  \ draw16: non-zero, not the rider's columns
d16_sc   = &1C
d16_row  = &1D
rl_off   = &1F                  \ restore_lines: the obstacle column, x 8
d16src   = &92                  \ draw16: the source column (2)
rb0      = &94                  \ draw16: the three rows, set back (2 each)
rb1      = &96
rb2      = &98
wlev     = &9A                  \ status.6502's
sp_player = &9B
dg_l     = &9C
dg_r     = &9D
dg_col   = &9E
dg_i     = &9F
dg_n     = &A0
dg_g     = &A1
dg_y     = &A2
skill    = &A3                  \ flow.6502: 0-5, A-F
joined   = &A4                  \ bit p: player p plays
winner   = &A5
cspr     = &A6                  \ cu_crash: the dead rider frame (3, 4)
hc       = &A7                  \ specials.6502: 4
top_put  = &AB                  \ compose_rider: the highest line put back
en_n     = &1E                  \ enemies on the list this field
d2       = &50                  \ 2: draw16's third character row
ts       = &52                  \ draw16: the tall sprite
dcol     = &53                  \ draw16: its screen column (0-76)
dt       = &54                  \ draw16: the window line of its top (0-24)
lena     = &55                  \ draw16: lines in its first character row
lenb     = &56                  \ draw16: lena + 8
newt     = &57                  \ the rider's top this field (window line)
pk       = &58                  \ 2: peek's pointer
rq       = &5A                  \ 2: respawn's column
oend     = &5C                  \ 2: an object's end
vfrom    = &5E                  \ vacated lines, from
vto      = &5F                  \ and to
ukind    = &60                  \ 4: the obstacle under rider column RIDER + c (&FF: none)
uoc      = &64                  \ 4: and which of its columns
fg_to    = &68                  \ fill_ground: the column to stop at
fg_byte  = &69                  \ and the byte
d0       = &70                  \ 2: the top character row at a column
d1       = &72                  \ 2: the character row below it
bas      = &74                  \ 2: this strip's obstacle row
gb       = &76                  \ 2: this strip's ground row
strip    = &78
obj      = &79
col      = &7A                  \ the object's screen column, signed (-32..79)
wid      = &7B
kind     = &7C
hit      = &7D                  \ non-zero: the rider's columns were written over
cc       = &7E                  \ a sprite column, 0-3
tmp      = &7F
keys     = &80                  \ 4: accelerate held, per strip (bit 7)
jumps    = &84                  \ 4: jump held, per strip (bit 7)
vec      = &88                  \ 2: a shift routine
bands    = &8A                  \ bands the raster has left this field (the T1 hook)
field    = &8B                  \ the field this pass of the loop is for
kn       = &8C                  \ the key being read
tmp2     = &8D

IRQ_UNINSTALL = 0

\ !BOOT (*EXEC, the disc's option 3): MODE 2 once, before the game loads, so that it never has to be
\ set again (decision 37); then the game.
SECTION boot, org = 0, filename = "!BOOT"
    EQUS "MODE2", 13, "*RUN DDD2", 13
ENDSECTION

SECTION ddd2, org = ORG_AT, load = LOAD_AT, exec = reloc - ORG_AT + LOAD_AT, filename = "DDD2"

    INCLUDE "../build/sprites.6502"     \ first: ORG_AT is a page start (make_data.py)

.start
    LDA #23 : JSR OSWRCH        \ VDU 23,1,0;0;0;0; - cursor off
    LDA #1  : JSR OSWRCH
    LDX #8
.cursor_off
    LDA #0 : JSR OSWRCH
    DEX
    BNE cursor_off
    JSR install_irq             \ IRQ1V ours from here on (the MOS's text output still serves)
    LDX #0                      \ page 8's code and the stack page's, from the file's tail (at
.start_copy                     \ its load address, above anything the move down wrote; MODE 2
    LDA p8_image - ORG_AT + LOAD_AT,X   \ has not yet cleared it)
    STA &0800,X
    CPX #p1_end - &0100
    BCS start_p1
    LDA p1_image - ORG_AT + LOAD_AT,X
    STA &0100,X
.start_p1
    INX
    BNE start_copy
    JMP title                   \ flow.6502

.loop
    LDA frames                  \ one pass a field: wait for one that has not had its pass
.wait_field
    CMP field
    BNE new_field
    LDA frames
    JMP wait_field
.new_field
    STA field
    INC pass_count              \ passes made (for the oracle; a field can be dropped)
    BNE nf_counted
    INC pass_count + 1
.nf_counted
    LDX #0
.strip_loop
    STX strip
.wait_band                      \ until bands >= strip + 1: the raster has left its window
    LDA bands
    BNE wb_band
    LDA strip                   \ bands 0: the next field, before its first band (line 120).
    CMP #3                      \ Strip 3 may start then: its window comes at line 240, 120
    BEQ band_left               \ lines (15,000 cycles) on. The others wait.
    BNE wait_band
.wb_band
    SEC
    SBC strip
    BEQ wait_band               \ (bands - strip - 1 < 0)
    BCC wait_band
    CMP #3                      \ but no more than two bands later (bands - strip <= 2): then
    BCC band_left               \ 208 lines or more (26,600 cycles) before the raster is back.
.too_late                       \ Later than that (the pass started late, after one that ran
    LDA bands                   \ over), wait for this field to end and the band in the next:
    BNE too_late                \ a field dropped, never a write in the window
    JMP wait_band
.band_left
    LDX strip
    BNE strip_go
    JSR status_update           \ before strip 0: the status line (status.6502)
    JSR read_keys               \ and this field's keys
    LDX #0
.strip_go
    JSR update_strip
.strip_done
    LDX strip
    INX
    CPX #4
    BNE strip_loop
.pass_end                       \ (every pass ends here: the oracle's check)
    JSR game_done               \ everyone out or finished: the game's end (flow.6502)
    JMP loop

\ read_keys: the eight keys into keys and jumps (bit 7 set: held).
.read_keys
.keys_go
    LDA #7
    STA kn
.rk_loop
    LDY kn
    LDX key_numbers,Y
    JSR keydown_int             \ A = &80 held, 0 not; X, Y clobbered
    LDY kn
    LDX key_slot,Y
    STA keys,X
    DEC kn
    BPL rk_loop
.keys_done
    RTS

\ the IRQ hooks (irq.6502)
.irq_vsync_hook
    INC frames
    BNE vs_count
    INC frames + 1
.vs_count
    LDA #0
    STA bands
    LDA #LO(T1_FIRST) : STA SYS_VIA_T1CL    \ (writes the latch's low byte)
    LDA #HI(T1_FIRST) : STA SYS_VIA_T1CH    \ load the counter and start
    LDA #LO(T1_NEXT)  : STA SYS_VIA_T1LL    \ then every band after it
    LDA #HI(T1_NEXT)  : STA SYS_VIA_T1LH
    DEC c8_tick                 \ the rotating colour: logical 8, one step every 3 fields
    BNE vs_done                 \ (update_rotating_colour_and_enemies, once a pass)
    LDA #3
    STA c8_tick
    LDX c8_step
    LDA c8_ulas,X
    STA &FE21                   \ the ULA's palette
    INX
    CPX #C8_STEPS
    BNE vs_step
    LDX #0
.vs_step
    STX c8_step
.vs_done
    RTS
.irq_timer_hook
    INC bands
    RTS

    INCLUDE "../../src/lib/irq.6502"
    INCLUDE "../../src/lib/keydown.6502"

\ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
\ update_strip: X = strip. One field of its rider: riding, or the crash and what follows.
\ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.update_strip
    LDA phase,X
    BEQ us_ride
    JMP crash_update
.us_ride
    LDA #0
    STA hit
    STA nspan                   \ nothing written over yet this field
    STA sp_all
    LDA finished,X
    BNE us_jump
    CLC                         \ pos += vel / 256 (the original moves, then accelerates)
    LDA pos_frac,X
    ADC vel,X
    STA pos_frac,X
    PHP
    LDA keys,X
    BPL us_coast
    LDA vel,X
    CMP #VMAX
    BCS us_speed
    INC vel,X
    BCC us_speed                \ (always: C clear from the CMP)
.us_coast
    LDA vel,X                   \ let go: slow by 1 a field (decision 24, PROPOSED)
    BEQ us_speed
    DEC vel,X
.us_speed
    PLP
    BCC us_jump                 \ under a column: nothing on the screen moves
    INC pos_lo,X
    BNE us_moved
    INC pos_hi,X
.us_moved
    LDA pos_lo,X                \ the rider at the finish: stop there (decision 22)
    CMP #LO(FINISH - RIDER)
    LDA pos_hi,X
    SBC #HI(FINISH - RIDER)
    BCC us_go
    LDA #1
    STA finished,X
    LDA #0
    STA vel,X
.us_go
    JSR level_check
    JSR wage_check
    JSR ground_edge
    JSR scroll
.us_jump
.prof_enemies                   \ (a label for the cost's breakdown: tools/verify_strips.mjs)
    LDX strip                   \ the enemies (enemies.6502)
    JSR enemy_clocks
    JSR enemy_levels
    JSR enemy_draw
.prof_rider
    LDA js,X                    \ the jump: from the ground with jump held; JUMP_FIELDS long
    BNE us_air
    LDA jumps,X
    BPL us_drawn
    LDA #1
    STA js,X
    BNE us_drawn
.us_air
    INC js,X
    LDA js,X
    CMP #JUMP_FIELDS + 1
    BNE us_drawn
    LDA #0
    STA js,X
.us_drawn
    JSR compose_rider
    JSR collide
    BCS crash_at
    RTS

\ crash_at: the rider has hit something (`cause`, from collide). The explosion where it was.
.crash_at
    LDX strip
    LDA #1
    STA phase,X
    LDA #0
    STA ct,X
    STA vel,X
    STA js,X
    LDA drawn_t,X
    STA crash_tt,X
    STA dt
    LDA #RIDER
    STA dcol
    LDA #TALL_EXPLOSION
    STA ts
    JMP draw16

\ scroll: X = strip, moved one column left. Every object on the screen moved; `hit` set if
\ anything was written over the rider's columns.
.scroll
    JSR set_bases
    LDA first,X
    STA obj
.us_obj
    JSR object_column           \ col; C set: past the right edge, stop
    BCC us_here
    RTS
.us_here
    BMI us_gone                 \ (N from object_column) gone off the left
    LDA kind
    BMI us_hole

    \ an obstacle. Across the edges: draw the columns on the screen. Anywhere else: its shift
    \ routine, which writes only the bytes that differ from the obstacle one column to the right.
    \ That is right everywhere but the rider's own four columns, where the screen held the rider
    \ and not the obstacle; those are drawn again after any write there (col RIDER-4 ..
    \ RIDER+3: the routine writes columns col .. col+4) - compose_rider.
    LDA col
    CMP #76
    BCS us_ob_clip              \ 76-79, or negative: part of it is off the screen
    TAX
    JSR set_dst
    LDY kind
    LDA shift_lo,Y : STA vec
    LDA shift_hi,Y : STA vec + 1
    JSR jump_vec
    LDA col                     \ what it wrote, columns col .. col + 4, for the enemies
    JSR add_span5
    LDA col
    SEC
    SBC #RIDER - 4
    CMP #8
    BCS us_next
    STA hit                     \ (0-7) the rider's columns are drawn again
    INC hit
    JMP us_next
.us_ob_clip
    JSR draw_clipped
    LDA col
    JSR add_span5
    LDA col
    CLC
    ADC #4
    CMP #80
    BCS us_next
    TAX
    JSR clear_column
    JMP us_next

    \ a hole: open col, close col + wid
.us_hole
    LDA col
    CMP #80
    BCS us_hole_close
    TAX
    LDA #0
    JSR ground_column
.us_hole_close
    LDA col
    CLC
    ADC wid
    CMP #80
    BCS us_next
    TAX
    JSR hole_ground             \ A = its level's ground
    JSR ground_column
.us_next
    INC obj
    JMP us_obj
.us_gone
    LDX strip
    LDA obj
    CMP first,X
    BNE us_next
    INC first,X
    JMP us_next

\ hole_ground: A = the ground byte for the hole `kind`'s level type (kind bits 5-6). X kept.
.hole_ground
    LDA kind
    LSR A : LSR A : LSR A : LSR A : LSR A
    AND #3
    TAY
    LDA ground_byte,Y
    RTS

\ level_check: X = strip. As the rider reaches each level's start (its left column at it, as
\ the original's initialise_level with player_x 0): its rider sprite becomes that level type's
\ (`rtype`; drawn again: `hit`), and at a sea level a take comes back if one has been lost
\ (consider_gaining_extra_take: level type 1, not level 1, not take 1). X kept.
.level_check
    CLC
    LDA pos_lo,X
    ADC #RIDER
    STA tmp
    LDA pos_hi,X
    ADC #0
    STA tmp2
.lc_loop
    LDA tmp
    CMP rl_lo,X
    LDA tmp2
    SBC rl_hi,X
    BCC lc_rts                  \ not there yet
    LDA #1
    STA hit
    INC rtype,X
    LDA rtype,X
    CMP #3
    BNE lc_type
    LDA #0
    STA rtype,X
.lc_type
    CMP #1
    BNE lc_next                 \ not sea
    LDA take,X
    CMP #2
    BCC lc_next
    DEC take,X
    LDA #1
    STA sdirty,X
.lc_next
    CLC
    LDA rl_lo,X
    ADC #LO(LEVEL_COLS)
    STA rl_lo,X
    LDA rl_hi,X
    ADC #HI(LEVEL_COLS)
    STA rl_hi,X
    JMP lc_loop
.lc_rts
    RTS

\ ground_edge: X = strip, just moved a column. The ground's colour changes at each level's start
\ (`nb`, the next one after column 0): its screen column, if on the screen, becomes the next
\ level's colour (the ground right of it already is; no hole is ever there: make_data.py's
\ course has none at a level's start). At column 0 the next level is the one at the left
\ edge: `ltype` steps on and `nb` to the level after. X kept.
.ground_edge
    SEC
    LDA nb_lo,X
    SBC pos_lo,X
    STA tmp
    LDA nb_hi,X
    SBC pos_hi,X
    BNE ge_rts                  \ 256 or more columns on
    LDA tmp
    CMP #80
    BCS ge_rts
    JSR set_bases
    LDY ltype,X                 \ the next level's type: ltype + 1, MOD 3
    INY
    CPY #3
    BNE ge_type
    LDY #0
.ge_type
    LDA tmp
    PHA
    TAX
    LDA ground_byte,Y
    JSR ground_column
    LDX strip
    PLA
    BNE ge_rts
    JSR next_level              \ at column 0
.ge_rts
    RTS

\ next_level: X = strip. The level at the left edge is the next one. X kept.
.next_level
    INC lidx,X
    INC ltype,X
    LDA ltype,X
    CMP #3
    BNE nl_type
    LDA #0
    STA ltype,X
.nl_type
    CLC
    LDA nb_lo,X
    ADC #LO(LEVEL_COLS)
    STA nb_lo,X
    LDA nb_hi,X
    ADC #HI(LEVEL_COLS)
    STA nb_hi,X
    RTS

\ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
\ the rider
\ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

\ compose_rider: strip `strip`. Its rider at this field's height, if that or what is under it
\ has changed: what is under the rider's columns (the obstacle there, lines 24-39), the sky
\ lines it has left black, then the rider. Sets newt.
.compose_rider
    LDX strip
    LDY js,X
    LDA #SKY
    SEC
    SBC jump_h,Y
    STA newt
    LDA hit
    BNE cr_go
    LDA newt
    CMP drawn_t,X
    BEQ cr_rts
.cr_go
    LDA newt
    CMP #SKY
    BNE cr_under                \ in the air: what is under it shows
    LDA drawn_t,X
    CMP #SKY
    BEQ cr_rider                \ on the ground, and was: it covers lines 24-39 itself
.cr_under
    JSR restore_under
    LDX strip                   \ the lines it has left, if sky: black
    LDA newt
    CMP drawn_t,X
    BCC cr_rose
    LDA drawn_t,X               \ fell (or stayed): drawn_t .. newt - 1
    STA vfrom
    LDA newt
    STA vto
    JMP cr_sky
.cr_rose
    CLC                         \ rose: newt + 16 .. drawn_t + 15
    ADC #16
    STA vfrom
    LDA drawn_t,X
    CLC
    ADC #16
    STA vto
    LDA vfrom                   \ the highest line put back: the vacated lines', or 24 (the
    CMP #SKY                    \ obstacles' rows, restore_under's)
    BCC cr_top
    LDA #SKY
.cr_top
    STA top_put
.cr_sky
    LDA vfrom
    CMP vto
    BCS cr_enemies
    CMP #SKY
    BCS cr_enemies
    JSR black_line
    INC vfrom
    JMP cr_sky
.cr_enemies                     \ enemies in its columns: drawn again over what was put back
    LDA erider
    BEQ cr_rider
    JSR enemies_over_rider
.cr_rider
    LDX strip
    LDA newt
    STA drawn_t,X
    STA dt
    LDA #RIDER
    STA dcol
    LDA rtype,X                 \ its level type's rider, in its colours (set_look)
    CLC
    ADC #TALL_RIDER
    JSR set_look
    STA ts
    JMP draw16
.cr_rts
    RTS

\ black_line: window line `vfrom` (sky) of the rider's four columns to black.
.black_line
    LDA vfrom
    LSR A : LSR A : LSR A
    LDX strip
    CLC
    ADC wix,X
    TAX
    LDA wrow_lo,X : CLC : ADC #LO(RIDER * 8) : STA pk
    LDA wrow_hi,X :       ADC #HI(RIDER * 8) : STA pk + 1
    LDA vfrom
    AND #7
    TAY                         \ the line in each of the four columns: Y, Y + 8, + 16, + 24
    LDA #0
    STA (pk),Y
    TYA : CLC : ADC #8 : TAY : LDA #0 : STA (pk),Y
    TYA : CLC : ADC #8 : TAY : LDA #0 : STA (pk),Y
    TYA : CLC : ADC #8 : TAY : LDA #0 : STA (pk),Y
    RTS

\ restore_under: strip `strip`. Lines 24-39 of the rider's four columns as the course has them:
\ the obstacle's column there, or black.
.restore_under
    JSR find_under
    JMP ru_draw

\ find_under: strip `strip`. ukind/uoc: the obstacle (and its column) under each of the rider's
\ four columns, &FF none; bas set.
.find_under
    LDA #&FF
    STA ukind
    STA ukind + 1
    STA ukind + 2
    STA ukind + 3
    LDX strip
    JSR set_bases
    LDA first,X
    STA obj
.ru_obj
    JSR object_column
    BCS ru_found                \ past the right edge
    BMI ru_next                 \ gone off the left
    LDA col
    BMI ru_cols                 \ (partly off the left: never under the rider, but harmless)
    CMP #RIDER + 4
    BCS ru_found                \ right of the rider: so is every object after it
.ru_cols
    LDA kind
    BMI ru_next                 \ a hole: not on these lines
    LDX #3
.ru_c
    TXA                         \ its column under rider column c: RIDER + c - col, if 0-3
    CLC
    ADC #RIDER
    SEC
    SBC col
    CMP #4
    BCS ru_cn
    STA uoc,X
    LDA kind
    STA ukind,X
.ru_cn
    DEX
    BPL ru_c
.ru_next
    INC obj
    JMP ru_obj
.ru_found
    RTS
.ru_draw
    LDA #0
    STA cc
.ru_col
    LDA cc
    CLC
    ADC #RIDER
    TAX
    JSR set_dst
    LDX cc
    LDY ukind,X
    BMI ru_black
    LDA uoc,X                   \ the obstacle's column: 8 bytes from uoc x 8 in each block
    ASL A : ASL A : ASL A
    STA tmp
    CLC
    LDA spr_top_lo,Y : ADC tmp : STA ru_top + 1
    LDA spr_top_hi,Y : ADC #0  : STA ru_top + 2
    CLC
    LDA spr_bot_lo,Y : ADC tmp : STA ru_bot + 1
    LDA spr_bot_hi,Y : ADC #0  : STA ru_bot + 2
    LDY #7
.ru_copy
.ru_top
    LDA &FFFF,Y
    STA (d0),Y
.ru_bot
    LDA &FFFF,Y
    STA (d1),Y
    DEY
    BPL ru_copy
    BMI ru_cnext
.ru_black
    LDA #0
    LDY #7
.ru_zero
    STA (d0),Y
    STA (d1),Y
    DEY
    BPL ru_zero
.ru_cnext
    INC cc
    LDA cc
    CMP #4
    BNE ru_col
    RTS

\ collide: strip `strip`, its rider drawn with its top at newt. The original's reads of the
\ screen (main_game_loop, check_for_collision, update_player). C set: a crash, `cause` saying
\ which: 1 right edge, 2 middle right, 3 top right, 4 under it in the air, 5 a hole.
.collide
    LDA #1
    STA cause
    LDA newt
    CLC
    ADC #15
    LDY #RIDER + 4
    JSR peek                    \ right_edge: the column right of it, its bottom line
    BEQ cl_mid
    CMP #&1F                    \ the gold's colour: collected, no crash (main_game_loop)
    BNE cl_hit
    JSR collect_gold
    BCC cl_hit                  \ (no gold there after all: lit, a crash)
    CLC
    RTS
.cl_mid
    INC cause
    LDA newt
    CLC
    ADC #8
    LDY #RIDER + 4
    JSR peek                    \ middle right
    BNE cl_hit
    INC cause
    LDA newt
    SEC
    SBC #1
    LDY #RIDER + 4
    JSR peek                    \ top right: the line above it
    BNE cl_hit
    INC cause
    LDX strip
    LDA js,X
    BEQ cl_ground
    LDA newt
    CLC
    ADC #16
    LDY #RIDER
    JSR peek                    \ in the air: the line under its left column
    BNE cl_hit
    CLC
    RTS
.cl_ground
    INC cause
    LDA #SKY + 16
    LDY #RIDER
    JSR peek                    \ on the ground: the ground under its left column
    BEQ cl_hit
    CLC
    RTS
.cl_hit
    SEC
    RTS

\ peek: A = window line (0-47), Y = screen column, strip `strip`. A = the screen byte, Z set
\ if 0.
.peek
    PHA
    LSR A : LSR A : LSR A
    LDX strip
    CLC
    ADC wix,X
    TAX
    CLC
    LDA wrow_lo,X : ADC col8_lo,Y : STA pk
    LDA wrow_hi,X : ADC col8_hi,Y : STA pk + 1
    PLA
    AND #7
    TAY
    LDA (pk),Y
    RTS

\ draw16: the tall sprite `ts`, its top at window line `dt` (0-24), screen columns dcol to
\ dcol+3 (dcol signed, -3 to 79: the columns off the screen are not drawn), strip `strip`;
\ whole, black included. A column's 16 lines are three runs: those in the first character row
\ (lines 0 .. 7-s, s = dt AND 7; through d0), the 8 in the next (d1), the s in the row after
\ (d2), each pointer set back so that Y is the sprite's line throughout, and the source
\ (d16src) the column's 16 bytes. The runs are unrolled, 13 cycles a byte: the first is entered
\ s steps in, the last 7 - s steps in (d16_ja, d16_jc: set once a sprite).
.draw16
    LDX ts
    LDA tall_lo,X
    STA d16src
    LDA tall_hi,X
    STA d16src + 1
    LDA dt
    AND #7
    STA tmp                     \ s
    ASL A : ASL A
    ADC tmp                     \ s x 5 (C clear: s < 8)
    ADC #LO(d16_A)
    STA d16_ja + 1
    LDA #HI(d16_A)
    ADC #0
    STA d16_ja + 2
    LDA #7 * 5                  \ (7 - s) x 5 = 35 - s x 5
    SEC
    SBC tmp : SBC tmp : SBC tmp : SBC tmp : SBC tmp
    CLC
    ADC #LO(d16_C)
    STA d16_jc + 1
    LDA #HI(d16_C)
    ADC #0
    STA d16_jc + 2
    LDA #8                      \ lena = 8 - s: the lines in the first row
    SEC
    SBC tmp
    STA lena
    CLC
    ADC #8
    STA lenb
    LDA dt                      \ the three rows' bases, set back: rb0 + s, rb1 - lena,
    LSR A : LSR A : LSR A       \ rb2 - lenb
    LDX strip
    CLC
    ADC wix,X
    TAX
    CLC
    LDA wrow_lo,X : ADC tmp : STA rb0
    LDA wrow_hi,X : ADC #0  : STA rb0 + 1
    SEC
    LDA wrow_lo + 1,X : SBC lena : STA rb1
    LDA wrow_hi + 1,X : SBC #0   : STA rb1 + 1
    SEC
    LDA wrow_lo + 2,X : SBC lenb : STA rb2
    LDA wrow_hi + 2,X : SBC #0   : STA rb2 + 1
    LDA #0
    STA cc
.d16_col
    LDA dcol
    CLC
    ADC cc
    CMP #80
    BCC d16_on
    JMP d16_skipcol             \ off the screen (negative, or right of it)
.d16_on
    TAY
    CLC
    LDA rb0 : ADC col8_lo,Y : STA d0
    LDA rb0 + 1 : ADC col8_hi,Y : STA d0 + 1
    CLC
    LDA rb1 : ADC col8_lo,Y : STA d1
    LDA rb1 + 1 : ADC col8_hi,Y : STA d1 + 1
    CLC
    LDA rb2 : ADC col8_lo,Y : STA d2
    LDA rb2 + 1 : ADC col8_hi,Y : STA d2 + 1
    LDY #0
.d16_ja
    JMP &FFFF
.d16_A
    LDA (d16src),Y : STA (d0),Y : INY
    LDA (d16src),Y : STA (d0),Y : INY
    LDA (d16src),Y : STA (d0),Y : INY
    LDA (d16src),Y : STA (d0),Y : INY
    LDA (d16src),Y : STA (d0),Y : INY
    LDA (d16src),Y : STA (d0),Y : INY
    LDA (d16src),Y : STA (d0),Y : INY
    LDA (d16src),Y : STA (d0),Y : INY
.d16_B
    LDA (d16src),Y : STA (d1),Y : INY
    LDA (d16src),Y : STA (d1),Y : INY
    LDA (d16src),Y : STA (d1),Y : INY
    LDA (d16src),Y : STA (d1),Y : INY
    LDA (d16src),Y : STA (d1),Y : INY
    LDA (d16src),Y : STA (d1),Y : INY
    LDA (d16src),Y : STA (d1),Y : INY
    LDA (d16src),Y : STA (d1),Y : INY
.d16_jc
    JMP &FFFF
.d16_C
    LDA (d16src),Y : STA (d2),Y : INY
    LDA (d16src),Y : STA (d2),Y : INY
    LDA (d16src),Y : STA (d2),Y : INY
    LDA (d16src),Y : STA (d2),Y : INY
    LDA (d16src),Y : STA (d2),Y : INY
    LDA (d16src),Y : STA (d2),Y : INY
    LDA (d16src),Y : STA (d2),Y : INY
.d16_skipcol
    LDA d16src                  \ the next column's 16 bytes (a tall sprite never crosses a page)
    CLC
    ADC #16
    STA d16src
    INC cc
    LDA cc
    CMP #4
    BEQ d16_rts
    JMP d16_col
.d16_rts
    RTS


\ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
\ the crash, and after it (kill_player)
\ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

\ crash_update: X = strip, A = its phase: 1 the crash, 2 respawn, 3 out of takes.
.crash_update
    PHA
    JSR enemy_clocks            \ the enemies' clocks run on (decision 28); X kept
    PLA
    CMP #2
    BNE cu_not_respawn
    JMP respawn
.cu_not_respawn
    BCC cu_crash
    RTS                         \ out: the dead rider stays where it lies
.cu_crash
    LDY ct,X
    CPY #CRASH_FIELDS
    BCC cu_on
    JMP cu_take
.cu_on
    LDA #TALL_DEAD              \ the dead rider's frame one
    STA cspr
    LDA #RIDER + DEAD_COL       \ after it flies: there, on the ground
    STA dcol
    LDA #SKY
    STA dt
    CPY #CRASH_FLY
    BCS cu_dead
    LDA crash_col,Y             \ flying
    CLC
    ADC #RIDER
    STA dcol
    LDA crash_t,Y
    STA dt
    CPY #0
    BEQ cu_draw                 \ the first: nothing of it to rub out
    LDA dcol                    \ moved: rub out where it was (the original's sprite_blank)
    CMP dead_col,X
    BNE cu_blank
    LDA dt
    CMP dead_t,X
    BNE cu_blank
    JMP cu_tick                 \ not moved: nothing new to draw
.cu_dead                        \ lying: frame one, two, one ... DEAD_FRAME fields each, a new
    TYA                         \ one drawn at each change (where the last flying one lay)
    SEC
    SBC #CRASH_FLY
.cu_mod
    CMP #DEAD_FRAME
    BCC cu_frame
    SBC #DEAD_FRAME
    PHA
    LDA cspr
    EOR #(TALL_DEAD EOR (TALL_DEAD + 1))   \ frame one <-> two
    STA cspr
    PLA
    JMP cu_mod
.cu_frame
    CMP #0
    BEQ cu_draw
    JMP cu_tick
.cu_blank
    LDA dcol : PHA
    LDA dt   : PHA
    LDA dead_col,X : STA dcol
    LDA dead_t,X   : STA dt
    LDA #TALL_BLANK
    STA ts
    JSR draw16
    PLA : STA dt
    PLA : STA dcol
    LDX strip
.cu_draw
    LDA dcol
    STA dead_col,X
    LDA dt
    STA dead_t,X
    LDY ct,X
    LDA cspr                    \ the dead rider's frame, in its colours
    JSR set_look
    STA ts
    JSR draw16
    LDX strip
.cu_tick
    INC ct,X
    RTS
.cu_take                        \ the crash is over: the next take, or out; the respawn
    CPY #CRASH_FIELDS           \ over three fields - erased; placed, its ground and look;
    BNE cu_place                \ the rest drawn (phase 2) - each light enough to share a
    INC take,X                  \ field with the other strips' worst
    LDA #1
    STA sdirty,X
    LDA take,X
    CMP #TAKES + 1
    BNE cu_erase
    LDA #3
    STA phase,X
    RTS
.cu_erase
    INC ct,X
    JMP erase_strip
.cu_place
    LDA #2
    STA phase,X
    JSR place
    JSR draw_ground
    LDX strip
    LDA rtype,X
    CLC
    ADC #TALL_RIDER
    JMP set_look

\ erase_strip: X = strip, still at the crash. Everything drawn above its ground to black: the
\ obstacles on the screen, the explosion, the dead rider. (The ground is drawn whole again, in
\ its levels' colours, by respawn.)
.erase_strip
    JSR set_bases
    LDA first,X
    STA obj
.es_obj
    JSR object_column
    BCS es_marks
    BMI es_next
    LDA kind
    BMI es_next                 \ a hole: the ground's, later
    LDA #0
    STA cc
.es_col
    LDA col
    CLC
    ADC cc
    CMP #80                     \ negative or past the edge: skip
    BCS es_cnext
    TAX
    JSR clear_column
.es_cnext
    INC cc
    LDA cc
    CMP wid
    BNE es_col
.es_next
    INC obj
    JMP es_obj
.es_marks
    LDX strip
    JSR erase_enemies
    LDA #TALL_BLANK
    STA ts
    LDX strip
    LDA crash_tt,X
    STA dt
    LDA #RIDER
    STA dcol
    JSR draw16                  \ the explosion
    LDA #SKY
    STA dt
    LDA #RIDER + DEAD_COL
    STA dcol
    JMP draw16                  \ the dead rider

\ respawn: X = strip, phase 2: placed, its ground drawn (cu_erase). The rest of it drawn.
.respawn
    LDA #0
    STA phase,X
    JSR set_bases
    JMP draw_objects

\ place: X = strip, its picture erased. Standing, at the first column past the crash with
\ CLEAR columns clear (decision 26); the levels and grounds it has reached. X kept.
.place
    CLC                         \ rq = the rider's course column
    LDA pos_lo,X
    ADC #RIDER
    STA rq
    LDA pos_hi,X
    ADC #0
    STA rq + 1
    LDA first,X
    STA obj
.rs_scan
    CLC                         \ the next object starts at rq + CLEAR or later: rq is clear
    LDA rq
    ADC #CLEAR
    STA tmp
    LDA rq + 1
    ADC #0
    STA tmp2
    LDY obj
    LDA obj_x_lo,Y
    CMP tmp
    LDA obj_x_hi,Y
    SBC tmp2
    BCS rs_found
    LDA obj_kind,Y              \ else, if it ends past rq, past it
    BMI rs_hole
    LDA #4
    BNE rs_wid
.rs_hole
    AND #&1F                    \ a hole's width (bits 5-6: its level type)
.rs_wid
    CLC
    ADC obj_x_lo,Y
    STA oend
    LDA obj_x_hi,Y
    ADC #0
    STA oend + 1
    LDA rq
    CMP oend
    LDA rq + 1
    SBC oend + 1
    BCS rs_next                 \ rq >= its end
    LDA oend
    STA rq
    LDA oend + 1
    STA rq + 1
.rs_next
    INC obj
    JMP rs_scan
.rs_found
    LDX strip
    SEC
    LDA rq
    SBC #RIDER
    STA pos_lo,X
    LDA rq + 1
    SBC #0
    STA pos_hi,X
    LDA #0
    STA pos_frac,X
    STA vel,X
    STA js,X
    LDA #SKY
    STA drawn_t,X
    LDA pos_lo,X                \ at or past the finish: finished (decision 22)
    CMP #LO(FINISH - RIDER)
    LDA pos_hi,X
    SBC #HI(FINISH - RIDER)
    BCC rs_first
    LDA #1
    STA finished,X
    LDA #LO(FINISH - RIDER)
    STA pos_lo,X
    LDA #HI(FINISH - RIDER)
    STA pos_hi,X
.rs_first                       \ first: past the objects now gone off the left
    LDA first,X
    STA obj
    JSR object_column
    BCS rs_drawn
    BPL rs_drawn
    LDX strip
    INC first,X
    JMP rs_first
.rs_drawn
    LDX strip
    JSR level_check             \ the levels the rider has reached
    JSR skip_grounds            \ the grounds it has passed, unpaid
.rs_levels                      \ and the one at the left edge
    LDA pos_lo,X
    CMP nb_lo,X
    LDA pos_hi,X
    SBC nb_hi,X
    BCC rs_placed
    JSR next_level
    JMP rs_levels
.rs_placed
    RTS

\ draw_strip: X = strip. The whole strip from scratch at its pos: the ground in each level's
\ colour, every object on the screen, the rider. Over black (MODE 2, or erase_strip).
.draw_strip
    JSR draw_ground
    LDX strip
    JMP draw_objects

\ draw_ground: X = strip. Its ground row, in each level's colour, whole (bas, gb set).
.draw_ground
    JSR set_bases
    SEC                         \ tmp2 = the next level's screen column, or 80
    LDA nb_lo,X
    SBC pos_lo,X
    STA tmp2
    LDA nb_hi,X
    SBC pos_hi,X
    BNE dw_far
    LDA tmp2
    CMP #80
    BCC dw_near
.dw_far
    LDA #80
    STA tmp2
.dw_near
    LDY ltype,X                 \ this level's ground to there
    LDA ground_byte,Y
    PHA
    INY                         \ the next one's after
    CPY #3
    BNE dw_next_type
    LDY #0
.dw_next_type
    LDA ground_byte,Y
    STA tmp
    LDA tmp2
    STA fg_to
    PLA
    LDX #0
    JSR fill_ground
    LDA #80
    STA fg_to
    LDA tmp
    JMP fill_ground

\ draw_objects: X = strip, its ground whole (bas set). Its holes, its obstacles, its enemies,
\ its rider.
.draw_objects
    LDX strip
    LDA first,X
    STA obj
.dw_obj
    JSR object_column
    BCS dw_end
    BMI dw_next
    LDA kind
    BMI dw_hole
    JSR draw_clipped
    JMP dw_next
.dw_hole
    LDA #0
    STA cc
.dw_hole_col
    LDA col
    CLC
    ADC cc
    CMP #80
    BCS dw_hole_next
    TAX
    LDA #0
    JSR ground_column
.dw_hole_next
    INC cc
    LDA cc
    CMP wid
    BNE dw_hole_col
.dw_next
    INC obj
    JMP dw_obj
.dw_end
    LDX strip                   \ the enemies, then the rider
    LDA #0
    STA nspan
    STA sp_all
    JSR enemy_levels
    JSR enemy_draw
    LDA drawn_t,X
    STA dt
    LDA #RIDER
    STA dcol
    LDA rtype,X
    CLC
    ADC #TALL_RIDER
    JSR set_look
    STA ts
    JMP draw16

\ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
\ objects and columns
\ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

\ object_column: obj's screen column for strip `strip`. Sets col, kind, wid.
\ Returns C set if it starts past the right edge (and so does every object after it); else C
\ clear, with N set if it has gone off the left (its last column, col + wid, is below 0).
.object_column
    LDX strip
    LDY obj
    LDA obj_kind,Y
    STA kind
    BMI oc_hole
    LDA #4
    BNE oc_wid
.oc_hole
    AND #&1F                    \ a hole's width (bits 5-6: its level type)
.oc_wid
    STA wid
    SEC
    LDA obj_x_lo,Y
    SBC pos_lo,X
    STA col
    LDA obj_x_hi,Y
    SBC pos_hi,X
    BEQ oc_right                \ 0..255 columns on
    CMP #&FF
    BNE oc_far
    LDA col
    CMP #&E0
    BCC oc_left                 \ more than 32 back: gone
    CLC
    ADC wid                     \ col + wid < 0: gone
    BMI oc_left
    LDA #0                      \ C clear, N clear: its last column is on the screen
    CLC
    RTS
.oc_far
    BMI oc_left
.oc_past
    SEC
    RTS
.oc_right
    LDA col
    CMP #80
    BCS oc_past
    LDA #0                      \ C clear, N clear: on the screen
    RTS
.oc_left
    LDA #&FF                    \ N set
    CLC
    RTS

.jump_vec
    JMP (vec)

\ set_bases: X = strip. bas, gb. X kept.
.set_bases
    LDA obase_lo,X : STA bas
    LDA obase_hi,X : STA bas + 1
    LDA gbase_lo,X : STA gb
    LDA gbase_hi,X : STA gb + 1
    RTS

\ set_dst: X = screen column. d0 = bas + column x 8; d1 = d0 + ROW.
.set_dst
    CLC
    LDA col8_lo,X : ADC bas     : STA d0
    LDA col8_hi,X : ADC bas + 1 : STA d0 + 1
    CLC
    LDA d0     : ADC #LO(ROW) : STA d1
    LDA d0 + 1 : ADC #HI(ROW) : STA d1 + 1
    RTS

\ draw_clipped: the obstacle `kind` at `col`, only its columns on the screen.
.draw_clipped
    LDA #0
    STA cc
.dc_loop
    LDA col
    CLC
    ADC cc
    CMP #80                     \ negative or past the edge: skip
    BCS dc_next
    TAX
    JSR set_dst
    LDA cc                      \ the column's 8 bytes start at cc x 8 in each block
    ASL A : ASL A : ASL A
    STA tmp
    LDY kind
    CLC
    LDA spr_top_lo,Y : ADC tmp : STA dc_top + 1
    LDA spr_top_hi,Y : ADC #0  : STA dc_top + 2
    CLC
    LDA spr_bot_lo,Y : ADC tmp : STA dc_bot + 1
    LDA spr_bot_hi,Y : ADC #0  : STA dc_bot + 2
    LDY #7
.dc_copy
.dc_top
    LDA &FFFF,Y
    STA (d0),Y
.dc_bot
    LDA &FFFF,Y
    STA (d1),Y
    DEY
    BPL dc_copy
.dc_next
    INC cc
    LDA cc
    CMP #4
    BNE dc_loop
    RTS

\ clear_column: X = screen column; its 16 lines, both character rows, to black.
.clear_column
    JSR set_dst
    LDA #0
    LDY #7
.cc_loop
    STA (d0),Y
    STA (d1),Y
    DEY
    BPL cc_loop
    RTS

\ fill_ground: the ground's four lit lines, columns X to fg_to - 1, to A (gb set). Returns X =
\ fg_to. About 50 cycles a column (ground_column, called for each, was about 90).
.fill_ground
    CPX fg_to
    BCS fg_rts
    STA fg_byte
    CLC
    LDA col8_lo,X : ADC gb     : STA d0
    LDA col8_hi,X : ADC gb + 1 : STA d0 + 1
    LDY #0
    LDA fg_byte
.fg_col
    STA (d0),Y
    INY
    STA (d0),Y
    INY
    STA (d0),Y
    INY
    STA (d0),Y
    INY : INY : INY : INY : INY \ the next column: Y + 8 from the first
    BNE fg_same
    INC d0 + 1                  \ (Y counts columns x 8, so it wraps exactly at a page)
.fg_same
    INX
    CPX fg_to
    BNE fg_col
.fg_rts
    RTS

\ ground_column: X = screen column, A = the byte for the ground's four lit lines (0: a hole).
.ground_column
    TAY
    CLC
    LDA col8_lo,X : ADC gb     : STA d0
    LDA col8_hi,X : ADC gb + 1 : STA d0 + 1
    TYA
    LDY #3
.gc_loop
    STA (d0),Y
    DEY
    BPL gc_loop
    RTS

\ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
\ per-strip state and constants
\ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
W0 = SCREEN + 4 * ROW           \ strip 0's window
WS = 7 * ROW                    \ one strip to the next
\ The per-strip constants (wrow, wix, obase, gbase, rider_tall) and the key tables are in
\ page &0D (make_data.py, low.6502), from these same numbers:
    ASSERT SCREEN = &3000 AND ROW = 640
.pos_frac   EQUB 0, 0, 0, 0
.pos_lo     EQUB 0, 0, 0, 0
.pos_hi     EQUB 0, 0, 0, 0
.vel        EQUB 0, 0, 0, 0
.first      EQUB 0, 0, 0, 0
.finished   EQUB 0, 0, 0, 0
.js         EQUB 0, 0, 0, 0     \ fields into the jump (0: on the ground)
.drawn_t    EQUB SKY, SKY, SKY, SKY     \ where the rider's top is drawn
.phase      EQUB 0, 0, 0, 0     \ 0 riding, 1 the crash, 2 respawn, 3 out of takes
.ct         EQUB 0, 0, 0, 0     \ fields into the crash
.crash_tt   EQUB 0, 0, 0, 0     \ where the explosion is (window line)
.dead_col   EQUB 0, 0, 0, 0     \ where the dead rider is drawn
.dead_t     EQUB 0, 0, 0, 0
.take       EQUB 1, 1, 1, 1     \ the original's `take`: 1-3, out at 4
.rtype      EQUB 0, 0, 0, 0     \ the level type the rider is in (0 land, 1 sea, 2 snow)
.rl_lo      EQUB LO(LEVEL_COLS), LO(LEVEL_COLS), LO(LEVEL_COLS), LO(LEVEL_COLS)   \ the next level's start, for the rider
.rl_hi      EQUB HI(LEVEL_COLS), HI(LEVEL_COLS), HI(LEVEL_COLS), HI(LEVEL_COLS)
.lidx       EQUB 0, 0, 0, 0     \ the level at the strip's left edge (0: level 1)
.ltype      EQUB 0, 0, 0, 0     \ the level type at the strip's left edge (column 0)
.nb_lo      EQUB LO(LEVEL_COLS), LO(LEVEL_COLS), LO(LEVEL_COLS), LO(LEVEL_COLS)   \ the next level's start after it
.nb_hi      EQUB HI(LEVEL_COLS), HI(LEVEL_COLS), HI(LEVEL_COLS), HI(LEVEL_COLS)
.c8_tick    EQUB 1              \ fields to the rotating colour's next step
.c8_step    EQUB 0
.cause      EQUB 0              \ the last crash's reading (collide)
.frames     EQUW 0
.pass_count EQUW 0

    INCLUDE "enemies.6502"
    INCLUDE "specials.6502"
    INCLUDE "flow.6502"
    INCLUDE "../build/data.6502"
.end                            \ the end of what runs at &0E00 up: below the screen
    ASSERT end <= SCREEN + 2048

\ What follows is only in the file. The tables for low RAM (&0400-&07FF, &0900-&0CFF; the RAM
\ hunt, docs/done.md): their bytes, with their labels set to where reloc puts them.
    INCLUDE "../build/low.6502"

\ Code and tables for page 8 and the stack page, assembled at their own addresses and written
\ here in the file; `start` copies them down (after install_irq: decision 32).
.p8_image
SECTION page8, org = &0800, guard = &0900
    INCLUDE "flow8.6502"
.p8_end
ENDSECTION
.p1_image
SECTION page1, org = &0100, guard = &01C0
    INCLUDE "flow1.6502"
.p1_end
ENDSECTION
.r0_image                       \ row 0, &3000-&327F: off the display (decision 37)
SECTION row0, org = SCREEN, guard = SCREEN + ROW
    INCLUDE "status.6502"
    INCLUDE "screen.6502"
.r0_end
ENDSECTION

\ reloc: runs at its LOAD address (exec), so only relative branches until the JMP, and its
\ addresses are load addresses (x - ORG_AT + LOAD_AT). First the low RAM images to their places
\ (nowhere near the file); then the program from LOAD_AT down to ORG_AT, a page at a time,
\ upwards: the destination is always below the source, and this routine is above all of it.
LOAD_OF_A = low_a_image - ORG_AT + LOAD_AT
LOAD_OF_B = low_b_image - ORG_AT + LOAD_AT
LOAD_OF_D = low_d_image - ORG_AT + LOAD_AT
LOAD_OF_R0 = r0_image - ORG_AT + LOAD_AT
.reloc
    SEI
    LDA #LO(LOAD_OF_A) : STA d0
    LDA #HI(LOAD_OF_A) : STA d0 + 1
    LDA #LO(LOW_A)     : STA d1
    LDA #HI(LOW_A)     : STA d1 + 1
    LDX #LOW_A_PAGES
    JSR reloc_pages - ORG_AT + LOAD_AT
    LDA #LO(LOAD_OF_B) : STA d0
    LDA #HI(LOAD_OF_B) : STA d0 + 1
    LDA #LO(LOW_B)     : STA d1
    LDA #HI(LOW_B)     : STA d1 + 1
    LDX #LOW_B_PAGES
    JSR reloc_pages - ORG_AT + LOAD_AT
    LDA #LO(LOAD_OF_D) : STA d0
    LDA #HI(LOAD_OF_D) : STA d0 + 1
    LDA #LO(LOW_D)     : STA d1
    LDA #HI(LOW_D)     : STA d1 + 1
    LDX #LOW_D_PAGES
    JSR reloc_pages - ORG_AT + LOAD_AT
    LDA #LO(LOAD_AT) : STA d0
    LDA #HI(LOAD_AT) : STA d0 + 1
    LDA #LO(ORG_AT)  : STA d1
    LDA #HI(ORG_AT)  : STA d1 + 1
    LDX #HI(end - ORG_AT + 255)
    JSR reloc_pages - ORG_AT + LOAD_AT
    LDA #LO(LOAD_OF_R0) : STA d0    \ row 0's code: after the move down, whose source covered
    LDA #HI(LOAD_OF_R0) : STA d0 + 1    \ &3000 (decision 37)
    LDA #LO(SCREEN)     : STA d1
    LDA #HI(SCREEN)     : STA d1 + 1
    LDX #3
    JSR reloc_pages - ORG_AT + LOAD_AT
    CLI
    JMP start
\ reloc_pages: X pages from (d0) to (d1). (A page past an image's end copies whatever follows
\ it in the file: harmless, inside the block.)
.reloc_pages
    LDY #0
.reloc_copy
    LDA (d0),Y
    STA (d1),Y
    INY
    BNE reloc_copy
    INC d0 + 1
    INC d1 + 1
    DEX
    BNE reloc_copy
    RTS
\ (The program's last page may copy a little past `end`, into the screen at &3000: harmless,
\ as `start`'s MODE 2 clears the screen. `end <= SCREEN` is the limit.)
ENDSECTION
